  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"1.9.0\"\n\npackage:\n  name: libtraceevent\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  - url: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/libs/libtrace/libtraceevent.git/snapshot/libtraceevent-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n    sha256: e6d82cb2392d04866203387fa092692e4282ccc36c8235dc129afd1ceba12684\n  # the BTF support needs a kernel >= 6.0 UAPI btf.h, newer than any\n  # conda-forge sysroot provides; used at build time only, not shipped\n  - url: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/stable/linux.git/plain/include/uapi/linux/btf.h?h=v7.1.4\n    sha256: 24cf19b4cc242a77e3c3149f243ad3f024e34e7ecd7bd156fb3997933f978be1\n    file_name: btf.h\n    target_directory: uapi-shim/linux\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip: not linux\n  dynamic_linking:\n    overlinking_behavior: error\n    overdepending_behavior: error\n  script:\n    - |\n      make -j\"${CPU_COUNT}\" \\\n        prefix=\"${PREFIX}\" \\\n        libdir_relative=lib \\\n        pkgconfig_dir=\"${PREFIX}/lib/pkgconfig\" \\\n        LDCONFIG=false \\\n        EXTRA_CFLAGS=\"${CFLAGS} -I${SRC_DIR}/uapi-shim\" \\\n        install\n    # conda-forge packages should not ship static libraries\n    - rm \"${PREFIX}/lib/libtraceevent.a\"\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - make\n    - pkg-config\n  run_exports:\n    - ${{ pin_subpackage('libtraceevent', upper_bound='x') }}\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      strict: true\n      lib:\n        - traceevent\n      include:\n        - traceevent/event-parse.h\n      files:\n        exists:\n          - lib/libtraceevent.so*\n          - include/traceevent/*.h\n          - lib/pkgconfig/libtraceevent.pc\n          - lib/traceevent/plugins/plugin_*.so\n          # rattler-build ships script-test files inside the package\n          - etc/conda/test-files/**\n  - script:\n      - pkg-config --exists --print-errors libtraceevent\n      - test \"$(pkg-config --modversion libtraceevent)\" = \"${{ version }}\"\n      # compile and run a program that allocates a tep handle, loads the\n      # shipped plugins (dlopen) and formats a trace_seq\n      - ${CC} test_program.c $(pkg-config --cflags --libs libtraceevent) -o test_program\n      - ./test_program\n    requirements:\n      run:\n        - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n        - pkg-config\n    files:\n      recipe:\n        - test_program.c\n\nabout:\n  summary: Linux kernel trace event library\n  description: |\n    libtraceevent is a library that parses the binary data of Linux kernel\n    tracepoint events and converts it into a human readable format. It was\n    originally part of the Linux kernel source tree (used by perf and\n    trace-cmd) and is now maintained as a standalone library.\n  license: LGPL-2.1-only AND GPL-2.0-only\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSES/LGPL-2.1\n    - LICENSES/GPL-2.0\n  homepage: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/libs/libtrace/libtraceevent.git/\n  documentation: https://www.trace-cmd.org/Documentation/libtraceevent/\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - chrisburr\n",
